==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{af|ru|от-|ходи́ть}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|отходи́ть}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-отходить.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|отходи́ть|impf|pf=отойти́}}

# to [[go away]], to go aside, to move away, to move aside
# {{lb|ru|military}} to [[withdraw]], to [[fall back]]
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to go away temporarily (with the intention to come back soon)
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to [[come around]], to come back to normal (e.g. after a shock or disease)
# to go out of fashion
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to [[recover]] (e.g. after a [[hangover]] or [[shock]])

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|impf-intr|4c|отходи́ть}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ru|отхо́д}}
* {{l|ru|отходня́к}}
